    "title": "WBC bracket: USA vs. Venezuela in World Baseball Classic championship",
    "text": "March 17, 2026Updated March 18, 2026, 12:24 a.m. ETDeeperDiveBETADeeperDive is a GenAI Answer Engine built for trusted publishers. It delivers clear answers and real-time content based on what people are reading now — showcasing various stories from the usatodaydemo Network that highlight not just what happened, but why it matters. This is currently a BETA being quality assessed by human beings. Mistakes may occur. Please reference surfaced articles to validate AI summaryWhere can viewers stream the USA versus Venezuela championship game?How did the United States reach the 2026 World Baseball Classic final?What is the broadcast time for the 2026 World Baseball Classic championship game?Follow WBC championship game live:Team USA vs. Venezuela updates and highlightsThe path taken by the United States to the 2026 World Baseball Classic championship game was not the smoothest this time, with a loss in pool play to Italy that featured postgame controversy related to manager Mark de Rosa's knowledge of the event's tiebreaker rules and nearly eliminated the Americans. Then came a nail-biting semifinal win over the Dominican Republic on Sunday, March 14, that ended on a controversial strikeout.Now that the USA persevered to make the WBC championship game for the third time, Venezuela awaits in a winner-take-all matchup in Miami on Tuesday, March 17. It used a late rally to beat Italy in the other semifinal on Monday in front of another raucous crowd.The U.S. last won the World Baseball Classic in 2017, when it beat Puerto Rico in the championship game. The Americans lost to Japan, 3-2, in the 2023 WBC championship game, which ended with Shohei Ohtani striking out Mike Trout.Here's a look at the updated 2026 World Baseball Classic bracket, as well as the schedule for Tuesday's championship game between the USA and Venezuela:World Baseball Classic bracket 2026QuarterfinalsDominican Republic 10, South Korea 0 (F/7) – March 13 in MiamiUnited States 5, Canada 3 – March 13 in MiamiItaly 8, Puerto Rico 6 – March 14 in HoustonVenezuela 8, Japan 5 – March 14 in MiamiSemifinalsUnited States 2, Dominican Republic 1 – March 15 in MiamiVenezuela 4, Italy 2 – March 16 in MiamiWBC championship gameUnited States vs. Venezuela – Tuesday, March 17 in Miami (BUY TICKETS)WBC scheduleAll times EasternTuesday, March 17 (championship game)Venezuela vs. United States, 8 p.m. in Miami (TV: FOX)",
